\subsection{Baseline}
Table~\ref{tab:baseline} reports the Restormer baseline, trained for the full
60-epoch cosine schedule and evaluated at its best-validation checkpoint
(epoch~57) on all 1111 test images.

\begin{table}[t]
\caption{Restormer baseline. GoPro test split, 1111 images, $256\times256$
center crops. Mean $\pm$ standard deviation across images.}
\label{tab:baseline}
\centering
\small
\begin{tabular}{@{}lccc@{}}
\toprule
Model & PSNR (dB) $\uparrow$ & SSIM $\uparrow$ & LPIPS $\downarrow$ \\
\midrule
Restormer (60 ep, ep.\ 57) & $28.937 \pm 3.857$ & $0.8661 \pm 0.0919$
& $0.1356 \pm 0.0841$ \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

Validation PSNR was flat across the final four epochs (28.884, 28.914, 28.907,
28.912; spread $\approx$0.03~dB) with the learning rate at $\eta_{\min}$,
indicating the run ended at a schedule-consistent optimum rather than being
truncated.

\textbf{This is not a Restormer reproduction.} The published GoPro result of
$\approx$32.9~dB uses full images and $\approx$300k iterations with a
progressive $128\!\rightarrow\!384$ crop schedule; ours uses 15{,}720 steps at a
fixed $128$~px crop and evaluates on $256$~px center crops. The gap is
explained by training budget and evaluation geometry, and the two numbers are
not comparable.

